      "note": "Serum triglycerides are a MIXTURE of triacylglycerols with different fatty-acid chains, so there is no single true molar mass. Clinical practice converts on the triolein (glyceryl trioleate) equivalent, and that is what is tabulated here. The value derived from triolein's formula is 88.545 mg/dL per mmol/L; the 88.57 widely quoted in online converters is not reproducible from triolein's molar mass under any published set of atomic weights, and is not used.",
