      "basis": "conventional",
      "note": "Blood urea nitrogen is reported on a NITROGEN basis, not as urea, so this is not the molar mass of any molecule: it is the mass of the two nitrogen atoms each urea molecule (CH4N2O, PubChem CID 1176) carries. The resulting 2.8014 mg/dL per mmol/L is therefore an atom count times an atomic weight, and never a compound's molar mass.",
